docs/cli.rst:8680: 139 chars: Once :ref:`installed <installation>` the tool should be available as ``sqlite-utils``. It can also be run using ``python -m sqlite_utils``.
docs/cli.rst:8690: 177 chars: The ``sqlite-utils query`` command lets you run queries directly against a SQLite database file. This is the default subcommand, so the following two examples work the same way:
