docs/cli.rst:8976: 134 chars: If your table contains binary data in a ``BLOB`` you can use the ``--raw`` option to output specific columns directly to standard out.
docs/cli.rst:9027: 147 chars: You can use the ``--functions`` option to pass a block of Python code that defines additional functions which can then be called by your SQL query.
docs/cli.rst:9040: 173 chars: Every callable object defined in the block will be registered as a SQL function with the same name, with the exception of functions with names that begin with an underscore.
docs/cli.rst:9080: 163 chars: You can attach one or more additional databases using the ``--attach`` option, providing an alias to use for that database and the path to the SQLite file on disk.
